> Do you have the values for what number means what branch, too? For  
> Slash'EM and Vanilla? So far I've only identified the two more common  
> ones (Mines and Planes).

The number of the branch depends on what order the branches are defined
in dungeon.def -file in the dat-dir.

For vanilla, starting from 0, the dungeons are DoD, Gehennom, Mines,
Quest, Sokoban, Ludios, Vlad's and Planes.

If we're in the planes, then the dungeon level number is negative and tells
what plane it is.


For Slash'em, starting from 0, the dungeons are DoD, Gehennom, Mines,
Quest, Lawful Quest, Neutral Quest, Chaotic Quest, Soko, Grund,
Ludios, Wyrm Caves, Sam's, Lost Tomb, Spider Caves, Sunless Sea,
Moloch's Temple, Giant Caverns, Vlad's, Frankenstein's, and the Planes.
(But note that I haven't tested this, I just looked at the
dungeon.def-file)

